{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-010", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s ACME Solar signs 300 MW/1,200 MWh PPA at $0.063/kWh", "content": "<p>Under the terms of the agreement, ACME Solar will deliver 300 MW/1,200 MWh of assured peak power supply through a firm and dispatchable renewable energy (FDRE) project combining solar and storage technologies.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/acme-solar-signs-ppa-with-seci-for-300-mw-1200-mwh-fdre-project-at-inr-6-kwh/\">India&#8217;s ACME Solar signs 300 MW/1,200 MWh PPA at $0.063/kWh</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/acme-solar-signs-ppa-with-seci-for-300-mw-1200-mwh-fdre-project-at-inr-6-kwh/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-011", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Taiwanese firm to make floating PV components in Philippines", "content": "<p>Taiwanese floating solar supplier Suntoward will begin producing floats, walkways and mooring components in the Philippines in early 2027.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/taiwanese-firm-to-make-floating-pv-components-in-philippines/\">Taiwanese firm to make floating PV components in Philippines</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/taiwanese-firm-to-make-floating-pv-components-in-philippines/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-012", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Politicians propose plug-in solar, batteries in Norway", "content": "<p>A group of Green Party politicians in Norway are calling on the Norwegian government to make it possible to connect plug-in solar and batteries that meet established safety requirements by the end of 2027.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/politicians-propose-plug-in-solar-batteries-in-norway/\">Politicians propose plug-in solar, batteries in Norway</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/politicians-propose-plug-in-solar-batteries-in-norway/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-013", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh plans 70 MW solar plant at coal power station", "content": "<p>The European Investment Bank (EIB) is expected to help finance a planned 70 MW solar power plant at Bangladesh’s Matarbari coal-fired power station, with commissioning targeted for December 2028.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/bangladesh-plans-70-mw-solar-plant-at-coal-power-station/\">Bangladesh plans 70 MW solar plant at coal power station</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/bangladesh-plans-70-mw-solar-plant-at-coal-power-station/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-014", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indonesian president instructs transformation of power utility", "content": "<p>A reform of Indonesia's power utility PT PLN is set to focus on improving efficiency and productivity, as well as accelerating the delivery of the country's 100 GW solar program.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/indonesian-president-instructs-transformation-of-power-utility/\">Indonesian president instructs transformation of power utility</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/indonesian-president-instructs-transformation-of-power-utility/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "longi-2026-10-19-015", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["longi"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["increase", "improve", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Longi researchers reveal how edge masking reduces recombination losses in solar cells", "content": "<p>Longi researchers found that edge masking improves the measured efficiency of heterojunction back-contact solar cells by suppressing edge recombination, with an optimal masking width of 5 mm. Their simulations suggest that selective metallization could further increase efficiency from 26.85% to a theoretical maximum of 27.39%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/longi-researchers-reveals-how-edge-masking-reduces-recombination-losses-in-solar-cells/\">Longi researche", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/longi-researchers-reveals-how-edge-masking-reduces-recombination-losses-in-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "jinko-2026-10-19-016", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["jinko"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "JinkoSolar unveils 28%-efficient back-contact TOPCon solar cell with amorphous silicon heterojunction passivation", "content": "<p>JinkoSolar has unveiled its first back-contact solar cell technology, combining TOPCon and heterojunction passivation in a new architecture called TAC. The Chinese manufacturer reported a peak cell conversion efficiency of 28%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/jinkosolar-unveils-28-efficient-back-contact-topcon-solar-cell-with-amorphous-silicon-heterojunction-passivation/\">JinkoSolar unveils 28%-efficient back-contact TOPCon solar cell with amorphous silicon het", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/jinkosolar-unveils-28-efficient-back-contact-topcon-solar-cell-with-amorphous-silicon-heterojunction-passivation/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-017", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sri Lanka asks PV system owners to disconnect after nationwide blackout", "content": "<p>Sri Lanka has ordered PV system owners to disconnect from the grid following a nationwide blackout on Oct. 17. The outage follows a similar incident in February 2025, when high solar penetration was identified as a major contributing factor.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/sri-lanka-asks-pv-system-owners-to-disconnect-after-nationwide-blackout/\">Sri Lanka asks PV system owners to disconnect after nationwide blackout</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/sri-lanka-asks-pv-system-owners-to-disconnect-after-nationwide-blackout/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-19-018", "date": "2026-10-19", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "100% renewables is doable, even in oil countries", "content": "<p>Oil- and gas-producing countries could strengthen their economies by accelerating domestic renewable energy deployment while maintaining fossil fuel exports, according to LUT University professor Christian Breyer. In an interview with <b>pv magazine</b>, he pointed to Norway as an example of how electrification can maximize the economic value of fossil fuel resources, while arguing that Russia's political choices are preventing it from exploiting similar opportunities.</p>\n<p>The post <a href", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/19/100-renewables-is-doable-even-in-oil-countries/", "type": "rss"}]}
